Description: GNOME System Monitor with the MaluOS tabs (GPUs, MaluOS Network, Queue)
 GNOME's process viewer and system resource monitor (Processes, Resources,
 File Systems), carried by MaluOS with its own tabs: GPUs (this computer's
 GPUs, the switch that shares them with the MaluOS network, the models
 loaded and the queue; the network's GPUs once the desk is enrolled), and,
 in later slices, MaluOS Network and Queue. The tabs render what the MaluOS
 session service publishes and compute nothing themselves; they appear only
 when that service answers, so on a plain GNOME desktop this is System
 Monitor as upstream ships it. Replaces Ubuntu's gnome-system-monitor
 package (same application id, same files).
